<title>UK: TENNIS-BRITAIN WIN DAVIS CUP TIE AGAINST EGYPT.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-BRITAIN WIN DAVIS CUP TIE AGAINST EGYPT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain beat Egypt 5-0 in their Davis Cup tennis Euro/African zone group two, third round tie on Sunday after taking both reverse singles.</p>
<p>Results (British names first):</p>
<p>Tim Henman beat Tamer El Sawy 6-7 (4-7) 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>Greg Rusedski beat Amr Ghoneim 6-4 6-2.</p>
</text>
